  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct IM re-assessments- 2022</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of countries with an up-to-date and followed up IM workplan</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-03-31" value="2" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: No update. Libya: an IM assessment was conducted and the main observation was that there is only 1 IM staff. This has caused LibMAC to find itself in a critical position. Despite being skilled, the IM staff is unable perform all IM tasks at the highest level. Unfortunately lack of funding and shortages of skilled staff has made it difficult to recruit. Iraq: Planning to conduct IM re-assessments by Q4 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq has been added as a target after a conversation with the Netherlands MFA.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct IM re-assessments- 2023</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of countries with an up-to-date and followed up IM workplan</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2023-03-31" value="2" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="0">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: no feedback. Iraq: We had initially planned to conduct an Information Management mission, but due to security concerns arising in the last quarter, the mission had to be canceled. However, this situation led to the establishment of a couple of remote IM support activities (such as meetings and workshop preparations with the head of the IM division in the DMA).
Libya: The IM assessment is scheduled to take place in the Q4 of this grant.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 - Afghanistan, Libya and Iraq</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq: No update Libya: Following with the workplan, GICHD with LIBMAC has implemented the TASK, EOD, EORE, and ACC-VIC modules, allowing operators (NGOs) to familiarize themselves with the system and address any issues that may arise during production and agreed with the following tasks completed by operators (NGOs):

All LR formed tested and verfied.
Validated migration mappings.
Conducted couple of online meeting with the operators (NGOs).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq: No update Libya: Following with the workplan, GICHD with LIBMAC implement the TASK, EOD, EORE, and ACC-VIC modules, allowing operators (NGOs) to familiarize themselves with the system and address any issues that may arise during production and agreed with the following tasks need to be completed by operators (NGOs):

Thoroughly verify all four forms involved.
Finalize translations.
Validate migration mappings.
Conduct a pre-go-live online meeting with the operators (NGOs).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct IM re-assessments - 2021</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of countries with an up-to-date and followed up IM workplan - 2021</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: Due to the security situation in Afghanistan the IM support in the country was suspended. 
Libya: following the work plan of IM support, the IM assessment was conducted based on the GICHD capacity development framework which is targeting four pillars (fitness for purpose of data, process, organization, and resources). The result of the previous assessment conducted in 2019 was 3.2 in total, while the current IM assessment is 3.0. The assessment revealed that the LiBMAC IM processes have not been reviewed since 2017, there is a lack of coordination with implementing partners on IM activities and the LibMAC IM team is severely understaffed.   However, the LibMAC IM Officer demonstrates a clear willingness to address some of those shortages; this becomes visible in strong involvement of the IM Officer in the IMSMA Core implementation and can be a perfect opportunity to reconnect with all the IM stakeholders.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="0">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordinating with both NMAA by Q2 to prepare the a workplan by addressing their requirements and needs, followed by an IM assessment for Libya and Afghanistan during Q4</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PM conducted several meetings with both NMAA of Libya and Afghanistan to set up the priority and needs of IM support and based on that two consultant contract has been issued in Q2 to support both NMAA and two workplans has been established in coordinating with NMAA of Libya and Afghanistan.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;After two consultant contract has been issued in Q2 to support both NMAA of Afghanistan.and Libya and two workplans has been established in coordinating with NMAA of Libya and Afghanistan.  and due to unforeseen circumstances which Afghanistan went through during Q3, we could not deliver your IM support based on the agreed work plan, therefore Afghanistan NMAC support has been suspended till farther notice.
While the IM support for Lybia is still provided based on the workplan.&quot;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
